  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q39-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "39",
    "prompt": "Given acute angles $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ such that $\\tan\\alpha=\\frac12$ and $\\tan\\beta=\\frac13$, find the exact values of the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q39-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{\\tan\\alpha+\\tan\\beta}{1-\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}\\\\\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{\\frac12+\\frac13}{1-\\frac12\\times\\frac13}\\\\\\tan(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{5/6}{5/6}=1.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q39-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}$",
          "worked": "Since both angles are acute, the given tangents give positive sine and cosine ratios:\n$$\\sin\\alpha=\\frac1{\\sqrt5},\\qquad \\cos\\alpha=\\frac2{\\sqrt5},$$\n$$\\sin\\beta=\\frac1{\\sqrt{10}},\\qquad \\cos\\beta=\\frac3{\\sqrt{10}}.$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\beta+\\cos\\alpha\\sin\\beta\\\\\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac1{\\sqrt5}\\frac3{\\sqrt{10}}+\\frac2{\\sqrt5}\\frac1{\\sqrt{10}}\\\\\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac5{\\sqrt{50}}\\\\\\sin(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q39-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}$",
          "worked": "Since both angles are acute,\n$$\\sin\\alpha=\\frac1{\\sqrt5},\\qquad \\cos\\alpha=\\frac2{\\sqrt5},$$\n$$\\sin\\beta=\\frac1{\\sqrt{10}},\\qquad \\cos\\beta=\\frac3{\\sqrt{10}}.$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\cos\\alpha\\cos\\beta-\\sin\\alpha\\sin\\beta\\\\\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac2{\\sqrt5}\\frac3{\\sqrt{10}}-\\frac1{\\sqrt5}\\frac1{\\sqrt{10}}\\\\\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac5{\\sqrt{50}}\\\\\\cos(\\alpha+\\beta)&=\\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      }
    ]
  },
